      "side": 1,
      "message": "I guess there is a point past which a broken bootloader is hopeless :)\n\nBut I guess something like would at least detect the problem (untested at this point):\n\n```diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c\nindex 6cc203816e5b..e9503cf97acb 100644\n--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c\n+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/pkvm.c\n@@ -85,6 +85,7 @@ static void __init sort_memblock_regions(void)\n static int __init register_memblock_regions(void)\n {\n        struct memblock_region *reg;\n+       bool pvmfw_in_mem \u003d false;\n\n        for_each_mem_region(reg) {\n                if (*hyp_memblock_nr_ptr \u003e\u003d HYP_MEMBLOCK_REGIONS)\n@@ -92,9 +93,18 @@ static int __init register_memblock_regions(void)\n\n                hyp_memory[*hyp_memblock_nr_ptr] \u003d *reg;\n                (*hyp_memblock_nr_ptr)++;\n+\n+               if (!pvmfw_size || pvmfw_in_mem)\n+                       continue;\n+               if ((reg-\u003ebase + reg-\u003esize \u003c\u003d pvmfw_base) || (pvmfw_base + pvmfw_size \u003c\u003d reg-\u003ebase))\n+                       continue;\n+               /* If the pvmfw region overlaps a memblock, it must a subset */\n+               if (pvmfw_base \u003c reg-\u003ebase || (pvmfw_base + pvmfw_size) \u003e (reg-\u003ebase + reg-\u003esize))\n+                       return -EINVAL;\n+               pvmfw_in_mem \u003d true;\n        }\n\n-       if (pvmfw_size \u0026\u0026 !memblock_overlaps_region(\u0026memblock.memory, pvmfw_base, pvmfw_size)) {\n+       if (pvmfw_size \u0026\u0026 !pvmfw_in_mem) {\n                if (*hyp_memblock_nr_ptr \u003e\u003d HYP_MEMBLOCK_REGIONS)\n                        return -ENOMEM;\n```\n\nThoughts?",
